+The socket is served from the main loop rather than from a thread. That is a deliberate
+trade — the library calls behind it are documented main-thread-only, and a reader thread would
+be a data race. Between ticks the loop waits on the socket itself, so a request is answered at
+once. The tick is 10 ms while a stream plays or the clock syncs, and 100 ms while the player is
+idle, so an idle player does not wake the CPU 100 times a second.
 
